---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
import { absoluteUrl } from '../lib/site';
// DRAFT: written from the public GitHub profile and the sdrtop docs. Rewrite it in your own voice.
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who writes this blog: a hobbyist from Hungary who builds Rust terminal tools."
  jsonLd={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Person',
    name: SITE.author,
    url: absoluteUrl('/about/'),
    sameAs: [SITE.links.github],
  }}
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Hi, I'm Viktor"
    lede="Hobbyist, which means nobody pays me for any of this and nobody can make me stop."
  />

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I'm Viktor Laszló, from Hungary. I mostly write Rust, mostly for the terminal, and I get
      a bit too excited about tools that show you what's really going on.
    </p>
    <p>
      My biggest project is <a class="external" href={SITE.links.sdrtop}>sdrtop</a>, a terminal
      monitor for software-defined radios. It draws spectrum and waterfall views, measures things
      instead of guessing them, and works over SSH. I test it against a HackRF One, an RTL-SDR
      and a tinySA Ultra.
    </p>
    <p>
      Between radio phases there are other obsessions that rotate in and out: homelab
      infrastructure, containers, and whatever comes next. This blog is where the logs and the
      write-ups end up, dead ends included.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to find me</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a class="external" href={SITE.links.github}>GitHub: {SITE.handle}</a></li>
      <li><a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a></li>
    </ul>

    <h2>About this blog</h2>
    <p>
      It is a static site with no trackers and no cookie banner. The source is on
      <a class="external" href="https://github.com/musithang/musithang.github.io">GitHub</a>, and
      the <a href="/projects/blog/">devlog</a> covers how it was built.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
